$script:P6Base = if ($env:LOCALAPPDATA) { Join-Path $env:LOCALAPPDATA 'DeepSeekComputerUse\dscu-driver' } else { Join-Path ([System.IO.Path]::GetTempPath()) 'DeepSeekComputerUse\dscu-driver' }
$script:P6Payload = @'
#=#=# FILE: docs/PROTOCOL.md
# dscu-driver-v1 protocol (NDJSON over `\\.\pipe\dscu-driver-v1`, alias `\\.\pipe\ds_computer_use_v7`)

One JSON object per line (UTF-8, LF), max 4 MiB per line. Responses are in request order per connection.

## Envelope (all three v7.1 client dialects are accepted, zero client changes)
| dialect | shape |
|---|---|
| `Invoke-DriverRpc` | `{"jsonrpc":"2.0","v":1,"action_id":N,"id":N,"method":"x.y","params":{..},"auth":"<token>"}` |
| `New-IpcEnvelope` | `{"v":1,"id":N,"method":"x.y","params":{..},"ts":ms,"action_id":N}` |
| `TryCallNamedPipe` (legacy) | `{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":N,"method":"x.y","params":{..}}` |

* `v` must be `1` (absent = legacy 1). `method` matches `^[a-z][a-z0-9_]*(\.[a-z][a-z0-9_]*)+$`.
* `auth`: token in `%LOCALAPPDATA%\DeepSeekComputerUse\driver.token` (per-user file). Without it only `driver.ping` / `driver.info` (minimal) answer.
* Response: `{"jsonrpc":"2.0","v":1,"id":N,"result":{..}}` or `{"..","error":{"code":N,"message":"KIND: text","data":{"kind":"KIND",..}}}`.

## Error kinds
| code | kind | meaning |
|---|---|---|
| -32700 / -32600 / -32601 / -32602 | PARSE_ERROR / INVALID_REQUEST / METHOD_NOT_FOUND / INVALID_PARAMS | JSON-RPC standard |
| 4001 | UNSUPPORTED_VERSION | `v != 1` |
| 4010 / 4011 | AUTH_REQUIRED / AUTH_FAILED | token |
| 4030 / 4031 | POLICY_DENIED / SECURITY_PATH_VIOLATION | allow-lists, path jail |
| 4040 | NOT_FOUND | window / notification |
| 4090 | IPC_IDEMPOTENT_REPLAY | same `action_id` + same request already executed |
| 4091 | IPC_STALE_ACTION_ID | `action_id` lower than the committed maximum |
| 4092 | IPC_STALE_HWND | `expect_hwnd` != foreground window |
| 4093 | IPC_STALE_REGION | `expect_fp` Hamming distance > 10 |
| 4094 | STALE_REF | snapshot expired / window closed or recycled / element gone (`data.reason`) |
| 4095 | AMBIGUOUS_TARGET | several windows/elements match (`data.candidates[]` with `window_id`) |
| 4220 | OUT_OF_BOUNDS | capture region outside the primary output (client falls back to GDI) |
| 4290 | MEMORY_FLOOR | available RAM < MemoryFloorMB (4096): large capture / sidecar refused |
| 5000 / 5010 | INTERNAL / PLATFORM_UNSUPPORTED | |

## Idempotency & optimistic locks
Only side-effecting methods (`uia.act`, `jab.act`, `notifications.dismiss`, `system.open_surface`, `input.*`) are checked.
`action_id > last` commits a new action; `== last` with an identical request is `IPC_IDEMPOTENT_REPLAY`, with a different request it is a sub-step of the same action; `< last` is replay (if seen) or stale.
`expect_hwnd` / `expect_fp` (params or top level) are evaluated before commit; a failed lock never consumes the `action_id`.
`ahash`: 48x32 gray (`(299R+587G+114B)/1000`) -> 8x8 block means -> bit *i* = block *i* > mean; 16 lowercase hex digits (bit-exact with `Get-RegionAHash`).

## Methods
`driver.ping|info|caps|shutdown` · `capture.frame|signature|ahash|bench` · `window.list|foreground` · `uia.snapshot|resolve|act` · `jab.windows` ·
`notifications.list|dismiss` · `system.open_surface` · `diag.spans|export|memguard|reset` · `sidecar.touch|status|unload`.

### capture.frame `{x,y,w,h,timeoutMs}` -> `{section,width,height,stride,format:"bgra8",backend,fresh,dirty_rects,move_rects,ahash,acquire_us,readback_us}`
`section` is a named file mapping (`Local\dscu-frame-<pid>-<slot>-<gen>`); map it directly (no pipe copy). Two alternating slots.
### uia.snapshot `{app|title|window_id, skeleton, depth, root:"@s8f3k2p9:e12", max_nodes, include_offscreen}`
Returns `snapshot_id`, `text` (compact outline with `@snapshot:eN` refs and `[+N children]` markers), `tokens_est`, `full_tokens_est`, `compression_pct`.
`skeleton` = 3 levels (override with `depth`); `root` drills into a ref of an existing snapshot (same ref namespace).
### uia.act `{ref, op: click|set_value|toggle|select|expand|collapse|scroll|focus, text?, headed?}`
Headless-first: UIA pattern when possible (`strategy:"uia_pattern"`, no mouse move, no focus steal); otherwise `strategy:"physical"` with a fresh validated `point` for DsNative61. `text` is never echoed or traced (only `text_len`).
### system.open_surface `{name}`: `notification_center|quick_settings|action_center|task_manager|settings[:page]|run|start|search|widgets|desktop|file_explorer`
