<#
.SYNOPSIS
  UIPI legal pass-through deployment for dscu-driver.exe (uiAccess="true").
.DESCRIPTION
  1. Creates a local code-signing certificate and trusts it in LocalMachine\Root + LocalMachine\TrustedPublisher.
  2. Injects a uiAccess="true" manifest with mt.exe, signs the binary with signtool.exe.
  3. Deploys it to %ProgramFiles%\DeepSeekComputerUse\ (a "secure location" - Windows refuses uiAccess elsewhere).
  Result: the driver can read/operate Task Manager, regedit and elevated terminals without running as Administrator.
  Security: the certificate is trusted machine-wide for CODE SIGNING; run -Uninstall to remove it again. The private key never leaves LocalMachine\My (non-exportable).
.EXAMPLE
  pwsh -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File .\setup-uiaccess.ps1 -DriverExe "$env:LOCALAPPDATA\DeepSeekComputerUse\dscu-driver\bin\dscu-driver.exe"
