"""WindowsAgentArena-compatible task runner + programmatic post-state verifiers + the 3 regression scenarios
distilled from the v10.0 runtime log (3 tasks, 0 completed).

Task schema follows WAA (`id`, `instruction`, `config`, `evaluator{func,result,expected}`) plus `max_steps_budget`.
The simulated desktops are *behavioural twins of the failure modes*, driven by a deliberately stubborn scripted
"LLM" that repeats exactly the mistakes the real model made in the log.  The system under test is the real
agent_brain (router, security policy, state machine, epoch guard, checkpoint) — only the world and the model are mocked.
"""
from __future__ import annotations

import asyncio
import math
